# AVI ELF II / Hyperboard 32K ROM; PRELIMINARY BUILD-ONLY CONFIGURATION.
# Distinct from the stock Elf2K and PicoElf configurations.
# A first-stage selection, not authorization to program an EEPROM.
#
# CPU logical address     Size    Content
# $8000-$97FF             6144    BOOTS monitor
# $9800-$A0FF             2304    AVI-specific HELP
# $A100-$A3FF              768    reserved (SEDIT omitted)
# $A400-$B0FF             3328    EDTASM
# $B100-$C1FF             4352    RESERVED (Visual/02 assembler crashes; deferred)
# $C200-$DBFF             6656    rc/BASIC L2
# $DC00-$EFFF             5120    reserved (Forth omitted)
# $F000-$F2FF              768    XMODEM
# $F300-$FFFF             3328    EBIOS / BIOS
#
# Proposed subdivision (NOT populated or committed to as ABI):
# $DC00-$E9AF: Netronics Tiny BASIC ROM payload (3504 B)
# $E9B0-$E9FF: alignment (80 B)
# $EA00-$EBFF: Tiny BASIC loader budget (512 B)
# $EC00-$EFFF: cassette / AVI helpers budget (1024 B)
#
# HISTORICAL VARIANT: remove rc/BASIC + XMODEM; Giant Monitor at F000.
# Q/EF4 default requires matching physical EF4 jumper and BIOS build.
# CDP1854 UART backend NOT IMPLEMENTED: inherited monitor/BIOS still
# contains Elf2K 8250/RTC/NVR/IDE assumptions.  CDP1854/CDP1863 port
# mapping is NOT VERIFIED.  This scaffold must not be used on hardware.
BOOTS=08000H
WARMB=($(strip $(BOOTS))+3)
RAMPAGE=07F00H

HELP=09800H
BIOS=0FF00H
EBIOS=0F800H
EDTASM=0A400H
GIANT=0F000H
# VISUAL=0B100H  # deferred: pinned Asm-02 segfaults in CI

# Deliberately disabled: VIDEO, PIXIE, SEDIT, FORTH, VISUAL.
